<Layouts.public flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user} return_to={@return_to}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <.header>
      Refund policy
      <:subtitle>A prepaid wallet, no expiries, no surprises.</:subtitle>
    </.header>

    <%!-- #140: the decided stance (2026-10-13) — non-refundable
        wallet balance, stated where the payment is made. The never-expiring
        balance is the fairness half. This template is the policy's one
        home: advisor wording tweaks land here (see
        docs/refund-policy.md). --%>
    <.card class="space-y-4" data-testid="refund-policy">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink" data-testid="refund-policy-stance">
        Wallet balance is non-refundable
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Money you add to your wallet can't be returned. There is no
        self-serve refund flow, and we don't issue refunds to payment
        methods.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The fairness half of that stance: your balance never expires.
        Money you add today is worth the same next year. We never expire,
        decay, or claw back a paid balance, and nothing is ever charged
        recurrently. A top-up happens only when you complete one yourself.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Chargebacks</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We keep the exposure structurally small: modest prepaid amounts,
        no recurring billing, and an exhausted balance suspends your
        instances instead of accruing debt. Nothing about this model can
        silently take your money.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Exceptions, at our discretion</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We can add funds to your wallet manually as goodwill: our mistake,
        a double charge, a genuine problem on our side. That's an exception
        we grant, not a refund channel to claim. It lands in your wallet,
        never as money back to a payment method, and a human decides each
        case.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        If a payment looks wrong, let us know before opening a chargeback.
        A goodwill credit is faster for both of us.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</Layouts.public>
